  "evidence": "The design was successfully planned and all individual blocks were drawn and verified against their expected values.\n1. `matching.sch`: L-type network boosted a 0.632 V amplitude 50 MHz sine wave to ~2.0 V amplitude.\n2. `bias.sch`: Diode-connected NMOS with 1 uA current source generated a DC bias of ~0.6 V.\n3. `splitter.sch`: Ideal balun with AC coupling and DC bias injection successfully generated differential signals centered at ~0.6 V.\n4. `rectifier.sch`: Differential cross-coupled CMOS rectifier successfully rectified the 2.0 V amplitude differential input to a DC voltage of ~2.08 V at VRECT_P and ~0.44 V at VRECT_N.\n5. `charge_pump.sch`: 3-stage Dickson charge pump successfully boosted the rectified voltage to ~4.4 V at VCP.\n\nHowever, the top-level testbench (`tb_iris.sch`) failed to netlist due to Xschem ERC errors (\"undriven node\" and \"shorted output node\"). I attempted to fix these by changing pin directions to `inout` and adding dummy resistors/voltage sources, but ran out of steps before resolving the top-level netlisting issue. Therefore, the full integrated system was not simulated.",
